@yes
on-arrival: right_dissent += 5; spd_bruning_support += 1; bruning_support += spd_seats; bruning_support_percentage += spd_r; bruning_undecided -= spd_seats; bruning_undecided_percentage -= spd_r; labor_opposition -= 35; industrial_opposition += 20; agriculture_opposition += 5; conservative_opposition += 40;
go-to: bruning_vote_of_no_confidence.spd_return

Despite some concessions to the Landvolkbewegung, some feel that our policies do not go far enough in helping German farmers, but the <span style="color: #000000;">**VdB**</span>  is satisfied with our handling of the situation. As such, the radical elements of the movement have been significantly empowered and will seek to use this initially moderate movement to resort to increasingly violent acts of protest. This will have a destabilising effect in the countryside and may serve to further radicalise the already disenfranchised rural electorate.

Meanwhile, Karl Hepp from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and disaffected regional affliates of the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span> have formed a new political party called the <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> in response to the preeminence of industrial interests in the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. With Hepp's position as President of the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span>, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> and the <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> have begun to wrangle for control over the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span> various regional chapters, which has severely compromised the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span>'s official stance of political neutrality. With its appeal as an <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> <span style="color: #909090;">**special interest**</span> party, this can only spell trouble for the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> in the upcoming elections

@no
go-to: bruning_vote_of_no_confidence.spd_return

Talks with the Landvolkbewegung have broken down due to our refusal to offer them any substantial concessions, much to the disapproval of the <span style="color: #000000;">**VdB**</span>. As such, the radical elements of the movement have been significantly empowered and will seek to use this initially moderate movement to resort to increasingly violent acts of protest. This will have a destabilising effect in the countryside and may serve to further radicalise the already disenfranchised rural electorate.

Meanwhile, Karl Hepp from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and disaffected regional affliates of the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span> have formed a political party called the <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> in response to the preeminence of industrial interests in the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. With Hepp's position as President of the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span>, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> and the <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> have begun to wrangle for control over the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span> various regional chapters, which has severely compromised the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span>'s official stance of political neutrality. With the growing strength of the Rural People’s Movement and the <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP's**</span> appeal as an <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> <span style="color: #909090;">**special interest**</span> party, this can only spell trouble for the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> in the upcoming elections
